#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186153395 :tutorial/content "**De Morgan's laws** for sets tell us alternative ways to represent the complement of a union or intersection.\n\n- De Morgan's law for unions states that $$\\overline{A \\cup B} \\equiv \\overline{A} \\cap \\overline{B}.$$\n- De Morgan's law for intersections states that $$\\overline{A \\cap B} \\equiv \\overline{A} \\cup \\overline{B}.$$\n\nIntuitively, you can think that the complement \"flips\" the union into an intersection and vice versa.\n\nTo demonstrate De Morgan's laws, consider the sets $A = \\{ 1,2,3 \\}$ and $B = \\{ 3,4 \\}$ in the universe $U = \\{ 1,2,3,4,5,6 \\}.$\n\n- Computing $\\overline{A \\cup B},$ we have $$\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A\\cup B} & =\\overset{―}{{1,2,3}\\cup {3,4}} \\\\ & =\\overset{―}{{1,2,3,4}} \\\\ & ={5,6}.\\end{aligned}$$ Computing $\\overline{A} \\cap \\overline{B},$ we have $$\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A}\\cap \\overset{―}{B} & =\\overset{―}{{1,2,3}}\\cap \\overset{―}{{3,4}} \\\\ & ={4,5,6}\\cap {1,2,5,6} \\\\ & ={5,6}.\\end{aligned}$$ So, we have that $\\overline{A \\cup B} = \\overline{A} \\cap \\overline{B}. \\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n- Computing $\\overline{A \\cap B},$ we have $$\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A\\cap B} & =\\overset{―}{{1,2,3}\\cap {3,4}} \\\\ & =\\overset{―}{{3}} \\\\ & ={1,2,4,5,6}.\\end{aligned}$$ Computing $\\overline{A} \\cup \\overline{B},$ we have $$\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A}\\cup \\overset{―}{B} & =\\overset{―}{{1,2,3}}\\cup \\overset{―}{{3,4}} \\\\ & ={4,5,6}\\cup {1,2,5,6} \\\\ & ={1,2,4,5,6}.\\end{aligned}$$ So, we have that $\\overline{A \\cap B} = \\overline{A} \\cup \\overline{B}. \\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$" :tutorial/id #uuid "df8a49e7-15bf-53b1-9af3-754dbf9fc0e8" :tutorial/math-academy-id 4366 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186153396 :tutorial/content "For the sets $A = \\{ 1,2,3 \\}$ and $B = \\{ 3,4 \\}$ in the universe $U = \\{ 1,2,3,4,5,6 \\},$ the region $\\overline{A \\cup B} = \\overline{A} \\cap \\overline{B}$ is shown below:\n\n![](images/36/367abce6d3386da347ab0eae5cb2d60110c3c642f7a679b6b8b8070e417fc10c.png)\n\nLikewise, the region $\\overline{A \\cap B} = \\overline{A} \\cup \\overline{B}$ is shown below:\n\n![](images/b0/b0a876470b3d2bd455395667f4d0221f73ee7c16dbbb20027a114c356638bc2d.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "3dc144c9-c8b9-50c4-a923-43e5b8574041" :tutorial/math-academy-id 4367 :tutorial/title "Venn Diagram Representations of De Morgan's Laws"}]}
